// Type checking for the tooling: scripts/ and the dev server. tsconfig.json
// includes only src/ and tests/, so before this file nothing compiled these at
// all — the code enforcing every invariant in the repo was the only code with
// no compiler over it.
//
// Three deliberate differences from the root config:
//
//   `strict: false` with `strictNullChecks: true`. Full strict reports 346,
//   163 of them implicit-any parameters. Annotating every callback in a tree of
//   AST walkers buys nothing a null check does not; the null checks are what
//   catch the bugs, so those are what is turned on.
//
//   `types: ["node"]` and the DOM lib. The root config lists only
//   `vite/client`, on purpose: putting node globals on src/'s type list would
//   let a browser module reach for `process`. The split keeps that intact. DOM
//   is here for the `page.evaluate` callbacks, which run in Chromium — eslint
//   scopes those globals to the five files that use them, and a tsconfig
//   cannot, so this is the one place the two disagree.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "checkJs": true,
    "strict": false,
    "strictNullChecks": true,
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["scripts/**/*.mjs", "server.mjs"]
}
